WEBVTT

NOTE EventClaim portal demo captions

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.856
Welcome to EventClaim, the Cursor Community portal for distributing partner credits at events.

2
00:00:05.856 --> 00:00:12.264
Before you run an event, complete the most important step: set up Luma and EmailJS in Settings.

3
00:00:12.264 --> 00:00:15.862
Open the Setup guide for step-by-step instructions.

4
00:00:15.862 --> 00:00:22.776
Add your Luma API key to sync checked-in guests, then connect EmailJS so claim emails can be sent.

5
00:00:22.776 --> 00:00:24.540
Save those values here.

6
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.686
They stay encrypted in this browser only.

7
00:00:27.686 --> 00:00:31.368
Once configured, you are ready to create events.

8
00:00:31.368 --> 00:00:38.328
The dashboard gives a quick overview across events — attendees, coupons, emails sent, and claim rate.

9
00:00:38.328 --> 00:00:41.784
Open Events to browse meetups or create a new one.

10
00:00:41.784 --> 00:00:43.733
Each event opens on Overview.

11
00:00:43.733 --> 00:00:52.200
Here you see live stats for attendees, offer types, emails sent, and claim rate, plus shortcuts into the rest of the workflow.

12
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.711
Scroll down for event configuration.

13
00:00:54.711 --> 00:01:02.592
Set the Notion claim guide, edit the claim page hero, and review status controls for draft, active, or completed.

14
00:01:02.592 --> 00:01:04.517
Auto-send emails is essential.

15
00:01:04.517 --> 00:01:12.792
Turn it on so attendees are emailed automatically as soon as they receive their coupon — no manual sending needed for each guest.

16
00:01:12.792 --> 00:01:17.280
CSV import is optional — only if Luma sync is unavailable.

17
00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:20.808
Attendees is where you will spend most of your time.

18
00:01:20.808 --> 00:01:25.896
Search and filter guests, and see coupon, email, and claim status together.

19
00:01:25.896 --> 00:01:29.472
Send, resend, or retry claim emails from the table.

20
00:01:29.472 --> 00:01:34.800
Open any guest for detail, and blacklist addresses you do not want to email.

21
00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:42.504
While the event is still in draft, create temp users with fake Cursor Credits links to verify claim emails before you go live.

22
00:01:42.504 --> 00:01:48.792
After an event, this page is your source of truth for who was invited, emailed, and who already claimed.

23
00:01:48.792 --> 00:01:52.251
Partner Offers is the other screen you will use most.

24
00:01:52.251 --> 00:01:56.688
Manage each partner coupon and track available versus granted links.

25
00:01:56.688 --> 00:02:02.640
Open an offer to review inventory, assigned attendees, and confirm the right credits went out.

26
00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:08.472
Keep offers organized here before and during the event so claim emails always have inventory ready.

27
00:02:08.472 --> 00:02:13.176
Audit Logs keep a short history of imports, emails, and claims.

28
00:02:13.176 --> 00:02:14.587
That is EventClaim.

29
00:02:14.587 --> 00:02:24.387
Set up Luma and EmailJS first, verify with temp users, use Overview auto-send, then run the event from Attendees and Partner Offers.

30
00:02:24.387 --> 00:02:25.872
Thanks for watching.
